<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dmitry Milyutin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">War Minister <a href="/years/1861">1861</a>–<a href="/years/1881">1881</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dmitry Milyutin was a Russian statesman who served as War Minister from 1861 to 1881. He carried out sweeping military reforms in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>, including the reorganisation of the army into military districts, improved officer training and the introduction of universal military service in 1874.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dmitry-milyutin.jpg" alt="Dmitry Milyutin" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andrey Denyer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Milutin_DA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
